i B2, Play F2, Play W3, Play W4, Play W8, Chi T3, Play T1, Play B2, Play W7, Play J1.\nThe game history of the previous player is: Play F2, Play F4, Play T1, Play J2, Play T8, Play W8, Play F3, Play W7, Play T9, Play B3, Play B1, Peng B9, Play W4, Play T8, Play W9, Play B8, Play F1, Play W4, Play W2, Play W3, Play W9, Play T5.\nThe followings are your valid actions:[Play T8; Play B5; Play B6; Play T6; Play B4; Play T5; Play T7]\u3002", "reasoning": "", "output": "Evaluation:\nLet me analyze my current hand and situation:\n\n**Current Hand:** T5, T6, T6, T7, T7, T8, B4, B4, B5, B5, B6\n**Exposed Meld:** [F3, F3, F3]\n\nI'm looking for patterns that can lead to a winning hand. Let me examine key possibilities:\n\n1. **T5-T6-T7-T8 sequence**: I have T5, T6(\u00d72), T7(\u00d72), T8. This could form chows like T5-T6-T7 and T6-T7-T8.\n\n2. **B4-B5-B6 sequence**: I have B4(\u00d72), B5(\u00d72), B6. This could form chows like B4-B5-B6.\n\n3. **Waiting structure analysis**:\n   - If I keep both Bamboo and Characters sequences, I'm working toward multiple chows\n   - With F3 pung already exposed, I need to maximize my winning chances\n\n**Key considerations:**\n- Unshown tiles show: T7(3 remaining), B4(3), B5(4), B6(3) - good availability\n- T5(2), T6(2), T8(1) - moderate availability\n- I need to maintain flexibility for drawing winning tiles\n\n**Promising moves:**\n- **Play T8**: Keeps T5-T6-T6-T7-T7, but loses the T6-T7-T8 potential. Maintains B4-B4-B5-B5-B6.\n- **Play T5**: Keeps T6-T6-T7-T7-T8, loses T5-T6-T7 but maintains T6-T7-T8 potential.\n- **Play B4 or B5**: Weakens the Bamboo sequence, less optimal.\n- **Play B6**: Keeps B4-B4-B5-B5, loses one chow potential but maintains pairs.\n\nThe strongest shape would be keeping maximum chow possibilities while maintaining pairs that could complete melds.\n\nReason:\nPlaying **T8** is optimal because:\n1. Only 1 T8 remains unshown, making it the least useful tile\n2. I retain T5-T6-T6-T7-T7 which can form T5-T6-T7 chow and still has a T7 pair\n3. I keep the complete B4-B4-B5-B5-B6 structure intact, which offers multiple winning possibilities\n4. This maintains maximum flexibility: I can wait for T4, T5, T6, T7, T8, B3, B4, B5, B6, B7 to improve my hand\n5. With 4 B5s still unshown and 3 each of B4, B6, B7, T7, my Bamboo sequence has excellent drawing potential\n\nAnswer: Play T8"}
